WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:05.609
Style, grace and elegance aren't terms usually
associated with modern American action movies.

00:00:05.609 --> 00:00:09.599
The genre is full of high-octane explosions,
brutality, and bloodshed.

00:00:09.599 --> 00:00:13.870
But when it comes to the craft of filmmaking,
they can often be unmemorable.

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:15.860
John Wick changed all that.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:20.930
The Keanu Reeves-led revenge thriller is epically
violent, but it's elegant violence, captured

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:23.150
in a way we don't get to see too often.

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:28.230
The character's sharp suits and sharper shooting
have left a huge mark on the action movie

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:32.390
landscape, including in a few ways you might
not yet have noticed.

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:36.250
Here's how John Wick rewrote the rules for
modern action.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:38.130
Low on ammo

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:42.281
To understand John Wick's influence on action
movies, you have to look at the state of the

00:00:42.281 --> 00:00:44.620
genre in the years before its release.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:48.751
Seven years after the The Bourne Ultimatum
rounded off its own influential trilogy, the

00:00:48.751 --> 00:00:53.440
genre felt tired, full of same-old structures,
and stale premises.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:58.010
There were occasional gems, like the old-man
action of the first Taken or the Indonesian

00:00:58.010 --> 00:00:59.420
import The Raid.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:04.430
But for the most part, mainstream Hollywood
action was plagued with insubstantial, CGI-heavy

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:05.449
spectacle.

00:01:05.449 --> 00:01:10.659
Success stories were frequently genre hybrids,
such as Lucy or Edge of Tomorrow.

00:01:10.659 --> 00:01:15.880
All-out action was reduced to the likes of
A Good Day to Die Hard or White House Down.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:20.630
Movies like these feel like half-baked efforts,
full of ridiculous spectacle that looks fake,

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:21.780
with no weight.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.799
Audiences were lulled into complacency.

00:01:23.799 --> 00:01:28.710
When John Wick came along and had the guts
to send a puppy to doggy heaven, people weren't

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:30.030
ready for the impact.

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:31.969
I know gun-fu

00:01:31.969 --> 00:01:36.679
John Wick's biggest asset is its energetic
implementation of gun-fu.

00:01:36.679 --> 00:01:41.890
A mixture of kung fu and gunplay, the cinematic
fighting style was first popularized by Hong

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:44.229
Kong action director John Woo.

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:48.649
Woo's movies helped create a subgenre of Heroic
Bloodshed.

00:01:48.649 --> 00:01:53.009
These stories feature characters who value
honor and integrity, and follow strict codes

00:01:53.009 --> 00:01:54.549
of ethics.

00:01:54.549 --> 00:01:59.000
Often the protagonists will stop at nothing
to exact revenge, with the resulting carnage

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:03.030
made more palatable by the sense of morality
we know they have.

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:06.509
John Wick is part of this tradition, but what
made it so different?

00:02:06.509 --> 00:02:12.430
Why did we become so attached to a blank slate,
nobody of a character we'd never met before?

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:18.600
"That f---ing nobody… is John Wick."

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:20.720
The dance of doom

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:25.280
Directors Chad Stahelski and David Leitch
made their marks in Hollywood as stuntmen,

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:29.950
most notably on the The Matrix, where Stahelski
performed as Keanu Reeves' stunt double.

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:33.860
This boots-on-the-ground perspective gave
the pair a unique perspective when it came

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:35.830
to shooting action as directors.

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:40.970
They saw that camera operators often regarded
action sequences as stressful exercises in

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:44.730
"hiding imperfections," so they rehearsed
and choreographed each scene with the camera

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:49.170
people included, leaving no room for surprises
when it came time to shoot.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:53.630
For authenticity, the duo was determined to
use as much footage of Reeves as possible.

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:58.370
The actor performed the vast majority of the
stunts himself, spending four months of pre-production

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:00.120
honing his techniques.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:05.870
Training included Japanese jiu-jitsu, Brazilian
jiu-jitsu, standing judo, and firearms training

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:08.150
designed for close-quarters combat.

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:13.400
The result is fight choreography that flows
freely in a kind of brutal ballet.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.860
Violence in John Wick is so stylized that
it comes off as a hypnotic dance, performed

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:22.120
by a professional hitman and his unfortunate
victims.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:23.600
Stylish shooters

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:28.980
John Wick proved the stuntmen-turned-directors
understand much more than just fight choreography.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:32.970
The cinematography of John Wick is as stylish
as the man himself.

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:37.480
Criminal underworlds are supposed to be murky,
gritty, full of dirt, yet Wick's world is

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:43.510
saturated in otherworldly hues, his fights
taking place inside of exclusive clubs, ornate

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:45.420
hotels, and mirrored museums.

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:47.860
The fights themselves are stylish, too.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:52.260
John Wick rejected the sharply edited, frantic
action that has come to be a crutch in the

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:53.260
genre.

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:58.410
Instead, wide shots and long takes capture
every punch, kick, and pistol whip.

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:03.300
You're left wanting to re-watch the movie
just to admire the ways its setpieces are

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:04.300
staged.

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:05.930
An underworld worth visiting

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:09.620
John Wick's world-building is unmatched in
the action genre.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:13.840
The story takes place within an intricate
network centering around the Continental,

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:18.319
a hotel in New York City which serves as a
safe haven for assassins.

00:04:18.319 --> 00:04:20.859
The universe is as detailed as it is original.

00:04:20.859 --> 00:04:25.920
Winston, the hotel's owner, is a charming
and affable enigma with evident power.

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:31.110
Outside of the hotel, special gold coins are
exchanged for criminals-only services from

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:33.810
seemingly legitimate businesses.

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:38.900
Tailors offer bulletproof suits, and sommeliers
are experts in pistols, instead of pinot.

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:44.090
It's an underworld you can feel intimately,
even if it's never all that explained.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:45.800
Fight like Wick

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:50.240
Years on from John Wick's release, the ripples
on the movie on the industry can be felt everywhere

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:51.360
you look.

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:55.300
Put simply, vengeance and well-done violence
are very "in."

00:04:55.300 --> 00:05:00.539
One heir of the style is Leitch's own Atomic
Blonde, a spiritual sibling to Wick.

00:05:00.539 --> 00:05:05.250
Charlize Theron as even said she was inspired
to dip into the Cold War-era action flick

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:07.689
because of her admiration for John Wick.

00:05:07.689 --> 00:05:11.819
Leitch then went on to up the action stakes
as director for Deadpool 2.

00:05:11.819 --> 00:05:17.279
Another John Wick producer, Basil Iwanyk,
has said the combat in the 2018 Robin Hood

00:05:17.279 --> 00:05:20.090
was inspired by Wick, saying to Collider,

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:24.580
"The stuff we're doing with the bow and arrow,
it's the same thing that Keanu does with the

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:25.580
gun."

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:30.240
The producers of the remake of cult classic
Highlander clearly have the same idea, hiring

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:34.400
Stahelski to apply Wick's style to that movie's
swordplay as director.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:39.740
In short, John Wick has inspired action filmmakers
to up their game, with highly-skilled assassin

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:42.180
flicks starring men and women both.

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:47.439
There's Jennifer Lawrence's Red Sparrow, Taraji
P. Henson's Proud Mary, and Jennifer Garner's

00:05:47.439 --> 00:05:52.229
Peppermint, a revenge thriller that's been
described as "John Wick with a female protagonist".

00:05:52.229 --> 00:05:54.840
"I will kill every one of you.

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:58.719
And then I'll pretty much wing it from there."

00:05:58.719 --> 00:05:59.900
Checking in?

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:04.900
John Wick's flair for world-building has also
spread across the action genre.

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:09.249
The Hitman's Bodyguard includes an assassin
underworld similar to Wick, and the Jodie

00:06:09.249 --> 00:06:14.139
Foster-starring Hotel Artemis has a premise
that's heavily reminiscent of The Continental.

00:06:14.139 --> 00:06:18.199
That movie stars Foster as the manager of
a hotel which doubles as a safe space for

00:06:18.199 --> 00:06:21.449
criminals to seek medical treatment and lay
low.

00:06:21.449 --> 00:06:26.139
In other words, the telltale marks of John
Wick are now everywhere, and there are no

00:06:26.139 --> 00:06:29.110
signs of the phenomenon slowing down.

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:34.580
Wick's stylish action has smashed the proverbial
sledgehammer into conventional genre fare,

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:36.449
unearthing a winning formula.

00:06:36.449 --> 00:06:40.979
The Boogeyman has changed the action movie,
and he's only getting started.

00:06:40.979 --> 00:06:42.180
Thanks for watching!

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:44.750
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
